  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A rectangular loop of sides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, carrying a current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, is placed in different orientations as shown in the figure below.<br />(a) <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/P_41_Option_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 134px;\" />&nbsp;(b) <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/P_41_Option_2.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 134px;\" /><br /><br />(c) <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/P_41_Option_3.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 133px;\" />&nbsp;(d) <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/P_41_Option_4.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 131px;\" /></p><p>If there is a uniform magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> in the positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> direction, in which orientations the loop would be in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math> stable equilibrium and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math> unstable equilibrium?</p>",
    "image": null
  },
